# Integration topology

Six function apps. One pattern. Why it works.

---

# The handoff / polling pattern

Every external integration follows the same two-function pair.

- **Handoff** = blob trigger. Pushes immediately when a file lands.
- **Polling** = timer trigger. Scans DB or upstream blob for changed records, builds CSV, uploads, updates `ImportsStatistics`.
- **`ImportsStatistics`** = the audit table. Every transfer recorded: filename, integration type, status, timestamps, source/destination.

```
Database change → Polling timer fires → builds CSV → uploads to staging blob
                                                      ↓
                                                  Handoff blob trigger
                                                      ↓
                                                  destination system (AH / FinOps / Workday)
```

*Net: outbound and inbound use the same shape. One mental model, six implementations.*

---

# The six function apps

Each speaks one external system. Each follows the same pattern.

<div class="cols three">
<div class="card">

### **CashHub-AH-DataSync**
Cash app, accruals, journals, products, split intake, comp actuals — all to and from Accounting Hub.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **CashHubAutomation**
Internal batch processing. Nightly accrual calc, auto-match, statement bulk import, mapping enrichment.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **MasterDataIntegrations**
Products + customers ingest from Mulesoft. Durable orchestration. Posts to FinOps and Workday.

</div>
</div>

<div class="cols three">
<div class="card">

### **CommonIntegrations**
The catch-all. FinOps↔AH bridges. Vendor / employee sync. Reference data seeding. Databricks queries.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **PrismIsolveIntegrations**
Prism invoices + cost files → Accounting Hub. Four functions. Simple.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **WorkdayIntegrations**
Payroll (both ways), time entries, project staffing, employee polling, invoices.

</div>
</div>

